Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 20:23:47 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 01/13] Mac Settings: macOS System Settings sidebar, window and
 navigation
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The sidebar is macOS's: the user's account, then macOS's groups with
coloured tiles (qml/Entries.js maps each entry to KDE pages). An entry
with several pages opens their list (LandingPage.qml), which drills in
with ‹ back. The window has no title bar (SettingsChrome, shared with
Golden Gate Finder): rounded, shadowed, glass sidebar with stoplights.
Page headers blend into the page with a bold title; no Help button and
no icons on the buttons.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
